speechtext:
Perhaps I had better read what the suggestion of the leader of the opposition was. It was as follows:
That clause 3, section 2, be amended by striking out the word "thirteen" in the first line thereof and substituting therefor "four";
That clause 2, subsection 5, be amended to read as follows:
"One member shall be appointed by the governor in council for each of the provinces of Canada to hold office during pleasure for such period not exceeding five years."
Is there any further discussion before I put the amendment moved by the hon. member for Fraser Valley, which reads:
(1)	That clause 3 be amended by the deletion of the word "fifteen" in paragraph (,1) and the substitution of the word "nineteen" therefor;
(2)	By the deletion of the word "thirteen" in paragraph (2) and the substitution of the word "seventeen" therefor;
(3)	By the deletion of all the words in paragraph (5) after the word "in" in line two and the substitution of the words "each of the nine provinces of Canada" therefor.
